\f0\fs24 \cf0 Working with aloha gourmet was a fun time in creating the island living eco goods product line. I was in charge of identity, packaging and art direction for this project. \
\
The need for this project was clear, Hawaii lacked a locally made and distributed eco goods line that was sold at an affordable price. I wanted to lean into two ideas for this project and give them a twist of my own in creating the identity and packaging for this. The first of two ideas were common design tropes typically associated with the word eco, which would be greens, plants and often times showcasing the natural product which would normally be a light beige or tan. The second idea was having packaging that reminded my audience of bright sunny Hawaii days, and what it\'92s like to live on the island.\
\
For the word mark I wanted keep something very modern and legible. I also to include some small curves to what could typically be blocked type to signal back to the recycling triangle and add natural organic feeling to what could be a regular sans serif Helvetica copy.\
\
Moving onto the packaging and the rest of the brand for island living eco goods, it was going to feature plants that are native and highly associated with Hawaii living. Monseratta leaves, banana leaves, hibiscus and plumerias are going to be the stars of this brand. Rich greens along with vibrant green to yellow gradients are going to own the majority of the visual field while a package will have a focus point in a bright yellow to burn orange gradient that will balance well with the product logo. \
\
